11
00:54:28,571 --> 00:54:34,571
Begin Again is a 2013 American musical comedy-drama film written and directed
by John Carney, and starring Keira Knightley and Mark Ruffalo.

12
00:59:25,714 --> 00:59:31,714
Knightley plays a singer-songwriter who is discovered by a struggling record label executive (Ruffalo) and
collaborates with him to produce an album recorded in public locations all over New York City.

13
01:04:22,857 --> 01:04:28,857
After the success of his 2007 musical film Once, Carney wrote the script in 2010
and employed Gregg Alexander to compose most of the film's music.

14
01:09:20,000 --> 01:09:26,000
With a US$8 million budget, production began in July 2012 with filming
taking place in various locations around New York City.

15
01:14:17,142 --> 01:14:23,142
The film premiered under its original title Can a Song Save Your Life?

16
01:19:14,285 --> 01:19:20,285
at the 2013 Toronto International Film Festival, and was released theatrically on June
27, 2014, in conjunction with the release of the film's soundtrack.

17
01:24:11,428 --> 01:24:17,428
It has grossed $63.4 million worldwide and received
mostly positive reviews from critics.

18
01:29:08,571 --> 01:29:14,571
It was nominated for an Academy Award for Best Original Song for "Lost Stars".

19
01:34:05,714 --> 01:34:11,714
The film explores themes of new york city, music recording,
singer-songwriter, street musician, city life.

20
01:39:02,857 --> 01:39:08,857
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
